WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:05.708
made by ph/ Rayan Mahmoud 
faculty of pharmacy , alexandria university

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:19.131
a stroke occurs when the blood flow
in part of your brain is blocked

00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:26.340
after just few minutes
 the starved brain cells begin to die

00:00:34.773 --> 00:00:40.125
normally the brain recieves blood 
via two major pairs of arteries

00:00:41.518 --> 00:00:44.229
which branch to   brain tissue

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:51.649
and supply your brain cells with 
a constant flow of oxygen , glucose and nutrients

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:55.026
necessary for their functions

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:05.401
in one type of stroke " ischemic stroke "

00:01:07.947 --> 00:01:10.782
an artery in your brain narrows

00:01:12.223 --> 00:01:17.065
or becomes completely blocked 
preventing normal blood flow

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:24.009
the blockage may be caused by blood clot also called a thrombus

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:27.371
which forms in unhealthy artery of the brain

00:01:30.211 --> 00:01:36.615
the lockup of blood flow causes the tissue
 the artery supplies to be come starved or ischemic

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:45.126
similarly the blochage may be due to " embolus " 
a blood clot that forms elsewhere in the body

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:49.439
and travels to the brain

00:01:54.288 --> 00:01:58.731
the embolus lodges in a narrowered artery and abstructs blood flow

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:14.966
immediate treatment for stroke may help minimize
 the brain cell injury and death

00:02:17.511 --> 00:02:19.335
if you have an ischemic stroke

00:02:21.265 --> 00:02:25.692
you may be given medication to break up
 the clot causing your stroke

00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:31.458
later your doctor may recommend surgery

00:02:32.853 --> 00:02:38.581
such as carotid endarterectomy to reduce your risk
 of having another ischemic stroke

00:02:39.151 --> 00:02:40.403
made by ph/ Rayan Mahmoud 
